# Docs must stay current

Documentation is part of the deliverable, not a follow-up. **Do not ship code changes that leave `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or `docs/*` stale.**

## When you change code, update docs in the same response

| If you change… | Also update… |
|----------------|--------------|
| Architecture, phases, layering, stack boundaries | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `AGENTS.md` if map/non-negotiables shift |
| Types, formulas, migrations, demo seeding | `docs/DATA-MODEL.md` |
| Crypto, storage keys, invites, threat assumptions | `docs/SECURITY.md` |
| Pull/push, SHA conflicts, session/local keys, commit messages | `docs/SYNC-AND-STORAGE.md` |
| UX copy, screens, shortcuts, visual tokens | `docs/PRODUCT.md` |
| Vercel/PWA/ports/Hobby deploy story | `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` |
| New risks, footguns, intentional behavior flips | `docs/AUDIT.md` (add/resolve finding) + relevant doc above |
| Top-level setup story or two-repo framing | `README.md` |

## Rules of engagement

1. **Same turn:** doc edits land with the code edit, not “we can document later.”
2. **Accuracy over volume:** rewrite the affected sections; don’t append contradictory notes.
3. **Rules too:** if a convention changes, update the matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.
4. **Trivial-only exception:** pure typo/formatting/refactors with zero user-visible or API behavior change may skip docs — when unsure, update docs.
5. **New modules/features:** add them to `AGENTS.md` map and the appropriate `docs/*` file before considering the task done.

If a change would invalidate an audit finding (e.g. fix demo seeding on first vault), mark it resolved in `docs/AUDIT.md` and correct `DATA-MODEL` / related rules.
